<span class="ltx_bibblock">DIALOGPT : Large-scale generative pre-training for conversational response generation.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In Asli Celikyilmaz and Tsung-Hsien Wen (eds.), <em id="bib.bib41.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: System Demonstrations</em>, pp.  270–278, Online, July 2020. Association for Computational Linguistics.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">doi: <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_Url ltx_ref_self">10.18653/v1/2020.acl-demos.30</span>.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-demos.30/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-demos.30/</a>.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proofs</h3>

<div id="Thmthm1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmthm1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Score Bounds &amp; Incentive Ordering)<span id="Thmthm1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthm1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DCS, as per Definition <a href="#Thmdefn1" title="Definition 1 (Distributional Correctness Score). ‣ 4.1 Definition and Interpretation ‣ 4 The Distributional Correctness Score ‣ Measuring Language Model Hallucinations Through Distributional Correctness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, under the assumption of default loadings (<math id="Thmthm1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{c}=l_{w}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{c}=l_{w}=1</annotation></semantics></math>), is bounded in the range <math id="Thmthm1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for any valid probability distribution. Let <math id="Thmthm1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=(p_{c},P_{W},p_{\textsc{idk}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=(p_{c},P_{W},p_{\textsc{idk}})</annotation></semantics></math> be such a distribution. Consider the following three canonical distributions:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{CC}=(1,0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{CC}=(1,0,0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (Confident Correctness).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{HA}=(0,0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{HA}=(0,0,1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (Honest Abstention).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{CI}=(0,1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{CI}=(0,1,0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (Confident Incorrectness).</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmthm1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, <math id="Thmthm1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{DCS}(\pi_{CI})&lt;\text{DCS}(\pi_{HA})&lt;\text{DCS}(\pi_{CC})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DCS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DCS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DCS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{DCS}(\pi_{CI})&lt;\text{DCS}(\pi_{HA})&lt;\text{DCS}(\pi_{CC})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p_{c},P_{W},p_{\textsc{idk}})=(p_{c}-P_{W})(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p_{c},P_{W},p_{\textsc{idk}})=(p_{c}-P_{W})(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})</annotation></semantics></math>. We want to find the global minimum and maximum of this function subject to a set of constraints.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The variables <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c},P_{W},p_{\textsc{idk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c},P_{W},p_{\textsc{idk}}</annotation></semantics></math> are probabilities or sums of probabilities, so they must be non-negative. Furthermore, the total probability assigned to the answer set <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot exceed 1. The domain <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by these constraints is a compact set in <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> (a tetrahedron). The function <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous on <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Extreme Value Theorem, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> must attain a global maximum and minimum on <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. These extrema can occur in the interior of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> or on its boundary.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will analyse the two factors of <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> separately. The term <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{c}-P_{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{c}-P_{W})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Since <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}+P_{W}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}+P_{W}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximum value of <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}-P_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}-P_{W}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> (when <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}=1,P_{W}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}=1,P_{W}=0</annotation></semantics></math>) and the minimum value is <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> (when <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}=0,P_{W}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}=0,P_{W}=1</annotation></semantics></math>). So, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1\leq(p_{c}-P_{W})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1\leq(p_{c}-P_{W})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. The term <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Since <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq p_{\textsc{idk}}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq p_{\textsc{idk}}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. The product is therefore also bounded:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-1\cdot 1\leq(p_{c}-P_{W})(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})\leq 1\cdot 1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1\cdot 1\leq(p_{c}-P_{W})(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})\leq 1\cdot 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1\leq\text{DCS}\leq 1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mtext>DCS</mtext><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1\leq\text{DCS}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that the score is bounded within <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now show that these bounds are sharp, </span><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text">, they can be achieved at specific points in the domain <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that three of these correspond to the stated canonical distributions. Checking the vertices of the tetrahedron <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Vertex 1: <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{c},P_{W},p_{\textsc{idk}})=f(0,0,0)=(0-0)(1-0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{c},P_{W},p_{\textsc{idk}})=f(0,0,0)=(0-0)(1-0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This corresponds to having confidence only in the complement of the answer set <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Vertex 2: <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\textsc{CC}}=f(1,0,0)=(1-0)(1-0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">CC</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\textsc{CC}}=f(1,0,0)=(1-0)(1-0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
This corresponds to perfect confidence in the correct answer and attains the maximum possible score.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Vertex 3: <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\textsc{CI}}=f(0,1,0)=(0-1)(1-0)=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">CI</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\textsc{CI}}=f(0,1,0)=(0-1)(1-0)=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
This corresponds to (summed) perfect confidence in the incorrect answer set and attains the minimum possible score.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Vertex 4: <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\textsc{HA}}=f(0,0,1)=(0-0)(1-1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">HA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\textsc{HA}}=f(0,0,1)=(0-0)(1-1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This corresponds to perfect confidence in abstention.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the function attains the values of <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> within the domain <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bounds are sharp. We have also shown, by direct calculation, that <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{DCS}(\pi_{CI})&lt;\text{DCS}(\pi_{HA})&lt;\text{DCS}(\pi_{CC})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>DCS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mtext>DCS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mtext>DCS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{DCS}(\pi_{CI})&lt;\text{DCS}(\pi_{HA})&lt;\text{DCS}(\pi_{CC})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcrl1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_crl">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcrl1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcrl1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Preference for Abstention-Hedging)<span id="Thmcrl1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcrl1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmcrl1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcrl1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmcrl1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}=(p_{c},P_{W1},p_{\textsc{idk1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk1</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}=(p_{c},P_{W1},p_{\textsc{idk1}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmcrl1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2}=(p_{c},P_{W2},p_{\textsc{idk2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk2</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2}=(p_{c},P_{W2},p_{\textsc{idk2}})</annotation></semantics></math> be two probability distributions over the answer space such that they satisfy the following conditions:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">They assign the same probability to the correct answer, with </span><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;p_{c}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;p_{c}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Distribution </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is more confident in incorrectness than abstention </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W1}&gt;p_{\textsc{idk1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk1</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W1}&gt;p_{\textsc{idk1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, whereas </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is more confident in abstention than incorrectness </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textsc{idk2}}&gt;P_{W2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk2</mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textsc{idk2}}&gt;P_{W2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The total probability assigned to the answer space </span><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is equal.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmcrl1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcrl1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the DCS of <math id="Thmcrl1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (abstention-hedging) is strictly greater than of <math id="Thmcrl1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (error-hedging).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">As a consequence of assumption (2), it follows that <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W1}&gt;P_{W2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W1}&gt;P_{W2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textsc{idk2}}&gt;p_{\textsc{idk1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk2</mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk1</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textsc{idk2}}&gt;p_{\textsc{idk1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For convenience, and without loss of generality, let <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W1}=p_{\textsc{idk2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk2</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W1}=p_{\textsc{idk2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W2}=p_{\textsc{idk1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk1</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W2}=p_{\textsc{idk1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{c}=l_{w}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{c}=l_{w}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle DCS(\pi_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle DCS(\pi_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(p_{c}-P_{W1})(1-p_{\textsc{idk1}})=(p_{c}-P_{W1})(1-P_{W2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk1</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(p_{c}-P_{W1})(1-p_{\textsc{idk1}})=(p_{c}-P_{W1})(1-P_{W2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle DCS(\pi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle DCS(\pi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(p_{c}-P_{W2})(1-p_{\textsc{idk2}})=(p_{c}-P_{W2})(1-P_{W1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk2</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(p_{c}-P_{W2})(1-p_{\textsc{idk2}})=(p_{c}-P_{W2})(1-P_{W1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and the difference is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=DCS(\pi_{2})-DCS(\pi_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=DCS(\pi_{2})-DCS(\pi_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(p_{c}-P_{W2})(1-P_{W1})-(p_{c}-P_{W1})(1-P_{W2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(p_{c}-P_{W2})(1-P_{W1})-(p_{c}-P_{W1})(1-P_{W2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{c}(1-P_{W1})-P_{W2}(1-P_{W1})-p_{c}(1-P_{W2})+P_{W1}(1-P_{W2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{c}(1-P_{W1})-P_{W2}(1-P_{W1})-p_{c}(1-P_{W2})+P_{W1}(1-P_{W2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{c}(1-P_{W1})-p_{c}(1-P_{W2})-P_{W2}(1-P_{W1})+P_{W1}(1-P_{W2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{c}(1-P_{W1})-p_{c}(1-P_{W2})-P_{W2}(1-P_{W1})+P_{W1}(1-P_{W2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{c}[(1-P_{W1})-(1-P_{W2})]+P_{W1}(1-P_{W2})-P_{W2}(1-P_{W1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{c}[(1-P_{W1})-(1-P_{W2})]+P_{W1}(1-P_{W2})-P_{W2}(1-P_{W1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{c}(P_{W2}-P_{W1})+P_{W1}-P_{W1}P_{W2}-P_{W2}+P_{W1}P_{W2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{c}(P_{W2}-P_{W1})+P_{W1}-P_{W1}P_{W2}-P_{W2}+P_{W1}P_{W2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{c}(P_{W2}-P_{W1})+P_{W1}-P_{W2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{c}(P_{W2}-P_{W1})+P_{W1}-P_{W2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(P_{W2}-P_{W1})(p_{c}-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(P_{W2}-P_{W1})(p_{c}-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W1}&gt;P_{W2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W1}&gt;P_{W2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W2}-P_{W1}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W2}-P_{W1}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}-1&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}-1&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=(\text{negative})\times(\text{negative})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>negative</mtext><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>negative</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=(\text{negative})\times(\text{negative})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DCS(\pi_{2})&gt;DCS(\pi_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DCS(\pi_{2})&gt;DCS(\pi_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmprop1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmprop1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmprop1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimal Guessing Threshold)<span id="Thmprop1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmprop1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmprop1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose a rational agent has a probability <math id="Thmprop1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}^{*}\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}^{*}\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> that its most likely answer is correct. The agent is only rewarded for providing a correct answer via an output distribution <math id="Thmprop1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=(p_{c}^{*},1-p_{c}^{*},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=(p_{c}^{*},1-p_{c}^{*},0)</annotation></semantics></math> if its score is greater than the abstention score of 0. This is true if and only if its confidence <math id="Thmprop1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds a specific threshold determined by the loadings:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}^{*}&gt;\frac{l_{w}}{l_{c}+l_{w}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}^{*}&gt;\frac{l_{w}}{l_{c}+l_{w}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmprop1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the default symmetric loadings (<math id="Thmprop1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{c}=l_{w}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{c}=l_{w}=1</annotation></semantics></math>), this threshold is <math id="Thmprop1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}^{*}&gt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}^{*}&gt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The agent’s output distribution if it chooses to guess is <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=(p_{c}=p_{c}^{*},P_{W}=1-p_{c}^{*},p_{\textsc{idk}}=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=(p_{c}=p_{c}^{*},P_{W}=1-p_{c}^{*},p_{\textsc{idk}}=0)</annotation></semantics></math>. The score for this output, assuming the answer is indeed correct, is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DCS(\pi)=(l_{c}p_{c}^{*}-l_{w}(1-p_{c}^{*}))(1-0)=(l_{c}+l_{w})p_{c}^{*}-l_{w}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DCS(\pi)=(l_{c}p_{c}^{*}-l_{w}(1-p_{c}^{*}))(1-0)=(l_{c}+l_{w})p_{c}^{*}-l_{w}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">A rational agent is incentivised to guess only if this score is greater than the score for abstention, which is 0, meaning that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(l_{c}+l_{w})p_{c}^{*}-l_{w}&gt;0\implies(l_{c}+l_{w})p_{c}^{*}&gt;l_{w}\implies p_{c}^{*}&gt;\frac{l_{w}}{l_{c}+l_{w}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(l_{c}+l_{w})p_{c}^{*}-l_{w}&gt;0\implies(l_{c}+l_{w})p_{c}^{*}&gt;l_{w}\implies p_{c}^{*}&gt;\frac{l_{w}}{l_{c}+l_{w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">For the default case <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{c}=l_{w}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{c}=l_{w}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the threshold becomes <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}^{*}&gt;\frac{1}{1+1}=\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}^{*}&gt;\frac{1}{1+1}=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves that DCS penalises correct answers from “lucky guesses” (low confidence) with a negative score, making abstention the more rational choice if the agent wishes to maximise its DCS.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmprop2a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmprop2a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmprop2a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Information-Theoretic Performance Bound)<span id="Thmprop2a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmprop2a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmprop2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop2a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random variable representing a query, <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be the random variable for its correct answer over a set of size <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be the training data of the model <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. The maximum expected DCS achievable by any such model is upper-bounded by a function of the mutual information between the answer and the training data, conditioned on the query:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{\mathcal{M}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D}}[DCS_{\mathcal{M}}(\pi(\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})]\leq f(I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝔔</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\mathcal{M}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D}}[DCS_{\mathcal{M}}(\pi(\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})]\leq f(I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmprop2a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop2a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔔</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the probability vector that model <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> produces the correct answer <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math> for query <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> given training data <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, and where <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is a monotonically increasing function such that as the conditional mutual information <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔄</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximum expected score <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(I)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(I)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(I)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(I)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmprop2a.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assuming <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{c}=l_{w}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{c}=l_{w}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximum DCS is bounded by <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DCS\leq l_{c}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DCS\leq l_{c}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, achieved when <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textsc{idk}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textsc{idk}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (equivalently, when <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textsc{idk}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textsc{idk}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W}=0</annotation></semantics></math>). Using the constraint that <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}+P_{W}+p_{\textsc{idk}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}+P_{W}+p_{\textsc{idk}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can replace <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W}</annotation></semantics></math> to write <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DCS=(p_{c}-P_{W})(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})=(p_{c}-(1-p_{c}-p_{\textsc{idk}}))(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})=(p_{c}-1+p_{c}+p_{\textsc{idk}})(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DCS=(p_{c}-P_{W})(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})=(p_{c}-(1-p_{c}-p_{\textsc{idk}}))(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})=(p_{c}-1+p_{c}+p_{\textsc{idk}})(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textsc{idk}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textsc{idk}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DCS=(2p_{c}-1)(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})=2p_{c}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">idk</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DCS=(2p_{c}-1)(1-p_{\textsc{idk}})=2p_{c}-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the maximum expected DCS is <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[DCS]\leq 2\mathbb{E}[p_{c}]-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[DCS]\leq 2\mathbb{E}[p_{c}]-1</annotation></semantics></math>. The expected correctness <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[p_{c}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[p_{c}]</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-P_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-P_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Bayes error rate. This gives <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[DCS]\leq 2(1-P_{e})-1=1-2P_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[DCS]\leq 2(1-P_{e})-1=1-2P_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fano’s inequality bounds <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> from below using the conditional entropy <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔔</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})\leq H_{b}(P_{e})+P_{e}\log_{2}(k-1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔔</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})\leq H_{b}(P_{e})+P_{e}\log_{2}(k-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{b}(P_{e})=-P_{e}\log_{2}P_{e}-(1-Pe)\log_{2}(1-P_{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{b}(P_{e})=-P_{e}\log_{2}P_{e}-(1-Pe)\log_{2}(1-P_{e})</annotation></semantics></math> is the corresponding binary entropy.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the relation <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})=H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q})-I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔔</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔄</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})=H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q})-I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔄</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> (meaning the data provides no information about the answer), the conditional entropy <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔔</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q};\mathcal{D})</annotation></semantics></math> approaches its maximum, <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>, </span><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.3" class="ltx_text">, the uncertainty remains maximal even after seeing the training data. Given this is the case (that there is no information in <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> about the true answer), we assume a uniform prior, <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q})=\log_{2}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathfrak{A}|\mathfrak{Q})=\log_{2}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, which means a high conditional entropy forces a high lower bound on <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>, approaching <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{e}\geq\frac{k-1}{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{e}\geq\frac{k-1}{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this high error rate into the DCS bound yields:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[DCS]\leq 1-2P_{e}\approx 1-2\left(\frac{k-1}{k}\right)=\frac{k-2k+2}{k}=\frac{2-k}{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[DCS]\leq 1-2P_{e}\approx 1-2\left(\frac{k-1}{k}\right)=\frac{k-2k+2}{k}=\frac{2-k}{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">For any problem with more than two answers (<math id="A1.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>), this bound is negative, while for binary problems (<math id="A1.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>) it equals zero. This demonstrates that as mutual information vanishes, the maximum achievable DCS becomes non-positive, consistent with the claimed functional dependence on <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔄</mi><mo>;</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝔔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathfrak{A};\mathcal{D}|\mathfrak{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Table of values for optimal guessing thresholds</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in §<a href="#S5" title="5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Measuring Language Model Hallucinations Through Distributional Correctness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, courtesy of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1 (Optimal Guessing Threshold). ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Measuring Language Model Hallucinations Through Distributional Correctness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we may set the loadings <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> to achieve a desired optimal guessing threshold, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.2 Table of values for optimal guessing thresholds ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Measuring Language Model Hallucinations Through Distributional Correctness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> provides some such examples, which fix <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{c}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{c}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and vary only <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
